uential Cdk5 and GSK3beta phosphorylation of CRMP2: implication of common phosphorylating mechanism underlying axon guidance and Alzheimer's disease. <source>Genes Cells.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>165</fpage>&#x02013;179.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15676027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Von Rotz, R.C., B.M. Kohli, J. Bosset, M. Meier, T. Suzuki, R.M. Nitsch, and U. Konietzko. <year>2004</year>. The APP intracellular domain forms nuclear multiprotein complexes and regulates the transcription of its own precursor. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>4435</fpage>&#x02013;4448.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15331662</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Yoshida, H., A. Watanabe, and Y. Ihara. <year>1998</year>. Collapsin response mediator protein-2 is associated with neurofibrillary tangles in Alzheimer's disease. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>9761</fpage>&#x02013;9768.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9545313</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib43"><citation citation-type="journal">Yoshimura, T., Y. Kawano, N. Arimura, S. Kawabata, A. Kikuchi, and K. Kaibuchi. <year>2005</year>. GSK-3beta regulates phosphorylation of CRMP-2 and neuronal polarity. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>137</fpage>&#x02013;149.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15652488</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib44"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, C., S.H. Kim, T. Ikeuchi, H. Xu, L. Gasparini, R. Wang, and S.S. Sisodia. <year>2001</year>. Characterization of a presenilin-mediated amyloid precursor protein carboxyl-terminal fragment gamma. Evidence for distinct mechanisms involved in gamma -secretase processing of the APP and Notch1 transmembrane domains. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>43756</fpage>&#x02013;43760.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11583985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib45"><citation citation-type="journal">Zheng, P., J. Eastman, S. Vande Pol, and S.W. Pimplikar. <year>1998</year>. PAT1, a microtubule-interacting protein, recognizes the basolateral sorting signal of amyloid precursor protein. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>95</volume>:<fpage>14745</fpage>&#x02013;14750.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9843960</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib46"><citation citation-type="journal">Zhu, X., Z. Sun, H.G. Lee, S.L. Siedlak, G. Perry, and M.A. Smith. <year>2003</year>. Distribution, levels, and activation of MEK1 in Alzheimer's disease. <source>J. Neurochem.</source> <volume>86</volume>:<fpage>136</fpage>&#x02013;142.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12807433</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>